{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== FINAL HANDOFF (session ending) ===\n\nDELIVERED: 3 of 6 stories of epic 1386, plus closing external blocker 1f32.\n- 35bc CLOSED, change 969 MERGED as 23e51a014.\n- 0a8c CLOSED, change 971 MERGED as 87478f047. Live store migration of 106 tickets complete; 0 tickets now carry an SC heading.\n- 2aa6 IN_PROGRESS, work COMPLETE and pushed as change 977 (commit 9bdafc942): LLM-Review +1, Verified PENDING at handoff, 0 unresolved comments. Local make test exit 0, lint + typecheck clean. Full step-by-step finish instructions are in a comment on 2aa6.\n- 1f32 CLOSED (--class plan_defect) on the original session's behalf with operator approval, after verifying its fix merged as 095c4afef and ADR 0053 grandfathering is live.\n- 93d0, 44c7 open and will unblock when 2aa6 closes; they are file-disjoint from each other (93d0 = eval_specs/eval_solver/gold_set, 44c7 = _guides/docs). 5f4d last.\n- Epic 1386 left in_progress. Do NOT close: 3 open children AND its attestation is stale (amending 35bc's and 2aa6's descriptions broke its plan-material-pin), so it needs a fresh review-plan.\n\nWORKTREE: ~/impl-ac-collapse, branch impl-ac-collapse, HEAD 9bdafc942 (= change 977). Gerrit rebases server-side, so use git reset --hard origin/main in the WORKTREE after 977 merges; never fast-forward the shared main checkout.\n\nARTIFACTS: migration restore files at /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-sc-migration-restore-2026-07-25.json and -stragglers.json.\n\nKEY FINDINGS FOR THE NEXT AGENT:\n1. Epic AC1 conflicts with 2aa6's deliberate exclusions - three live files under src/rebar/ legitimately keep the SC string (plan_review_T2.md's trial-metrics English, and the dod_uncertifiable wording in plan_review_verifier.md + _agentic.md). Epic AC1 must gain those carve-outs or the epic cannot honestly close.\n2. FOUR over-broad blanket-string ACs so far (35bc AC1+AC3, 2aa6 AC1+AC3), each amended mid-implementation at the cost of a re-review. 5f4d will very likely hit the same, since it IS the allowlist story.\n3. Two real defects reached live data in 0a8c and were caught by verification against the real store, not by tests: order-sensitivity (would have corrupted 97 of 104 tickets) and exact-match heading detection (silently skipped 2). Dry-run against real data before any store write - it paid for itself twice.\n\nMETHOD: every code leaf RED-first with the implementer held out from the edge/E2E oracle; oracles 12/12, 27/27 and 10/10 green; all mutations killed. No test was ever weakened to make a change land."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785018406062578001,"uuid":"28d212d9-d38a-488e-96d0-026daa7aaa1a"}